{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaWritheConstantB","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaWritheConstantB","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.constant_b_from_writhe_proportional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.constant_b_from_writhe_proportional","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaWritheConstantB.lean#L46-L60","doc":"**The constancy mechanism (proved; the proportionality is the hypothesis).**\nModel the residual as `r Z N = base(Z+N) + κ·(Z−N)` — an isoscalar baseline plus\nan isovector term *linear in `Z−N` with an `A`-independent coefficient `κ`* (the\nstructural ansatz suggested by the writhe's universal isospin slope). Then the\nmirror difference is `2κ·(Z−N)`, with `κ` the **A-independent** slope: this is\nexactly why the measured `b` (= the per-`T₃` slope = `4κ`) is constant in `A`.\n\nThe file asserts nothing about the value of `κ` (the open per-writhe coefficient,\n`κ = b/4 ≈ −0.437`); only that *if* the odd part is writhe-proportional with\nA-independent `κ`, the mirror slope cannot depend on `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.writhe_isovector_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.writhe_isovector_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaWritheConstantB.lean#L40-L44","doc":"The isovector (odd, `Z↔N`-antisymmetric) part of the writhe is `2(Z−N)`, and\nits mirror difference `4(Z−N)` carries NO `A`-dependence — the slope in the\nisospin variable is the same at every mass number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.writhe_isospin_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.writhe_isospin_split","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaWritheConstantB.lean#L34-L38","doc":"**Derived.** The writhe `4Z` splits into an isoscalar part `2(Z+N) = 2A` and\nan isovector part `2(Z−N) = 4T₃`. The isovector coefficient is the constant `2`\n(per unit `Z−N`) — UNIVERSAL, independent of `A`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}